{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793580030,"nonce":"ewyCbPM3ubgoLdlbnaVN/bj1+kk=","message":"Cause found: the failure comes from running the gates under `nohup`. nohup sets SIGHUP to ignored and a child shell inherits that, so the row `{\"kill -s HUP $$\", \"signal\", 1}` (files.lua:762) sees the shell survive and `assert(not x and y == v[2])` fails. Every failing NUC run in this issue was started with `nohup ... \u0026` (a background gate script, a loop script); every run started from an ssh session directly, without nohup, passed (46 of 46 and 3 of 3 for official_complete alone). Linux CI does not run under nohup, which is why it passes there. Start long NUC runs with `setsid` instead, which does not change signal dispositions. Not a zylua bug.","files":null}]}